\markup { \fontsize #6 \bold "Eight Measure Form" }

\markup \vspace #0.4

\markup { 
  These forms are centred around 'sentences' and 'periods'.
}

\markup \vspace #0.4

\markup \wordwrap {
  Sentences have two subphrases: presentation + continuation. The presentation consists of the basic idea and repetition. Continuation has the same length as presentation. In addition, it typically has 4 key traits: fragmentation, more rhythmic activity, sequences, faster harmonic rhythm.
}

\markup \vspace #0.4

\markup \wordwrap {
  Periods have two subphrases (antecedent + consequent), each consisting of a basic idea and contrasting idea. The antecedent ends in a weaker cadence, while the consequent ends in a stronger cadence. In other words, the antecedent asks, and the consequent answers.
}

